source: tests/help_pages.rs
description: "a command's -h and --help pages as this build renders them at 100 columns without color; any change to an about, a flag, a value, a heading or the layout changes them: review with cargo insta review, or re-accept with INSTA_UPDATE=always cargo test --test integration help_pages:: and review git diff tests/snapshots/"
---
==> omaddons backup restore -h <==
Restore WTF/, or one addon's settings, from a backup

Usage: omaddons backup restore [OPTIONS] <ID>

Arguments:
  <ID>  The backup: its id, or a prefix of 8 or more characters

Options:
      --addon <ADDON>  Only this addon's settings: its name, ref or a folder (repeatable)

Examples:
  omaddons backup restore 01M6Q2VA --dry-run  what it would put back
  omaddons backup restore 01M6Q2VA --addon WeakAuras
                                              one addon's settings only

Global: -t <TARGET>  --json  --dry-run  -v  --quiet  --no-color  --offline  (--help lists them all)
==> omaddons backup restore --help <==
Restore WTF/, or one addon's settings, from a backup

The whole WTF/ (keybindings, macros, every addon's settings), or with --addon one addon's settings
only. Undoable.

Usage: omaddons backup restore [OPTIONS] <ID>

Arguments:
  <ID>
          The backup: its id, or a prefix of 8 or more characters

Options:
      --addon <ADDON>
          Only this addon's settings: its name, ref or a folder (repeatable)
          
          folder:<F> names one folder alone.

Examples:
  omaddons backup restore 01M6Q2VA --dry-run   what it would put back, and its token
  omaddons backup restore 01M6Q2VA -t retail
  omaddons backup restore 01M6Q2VA -t retail --addon WeakAuras   one addon's settings
  omaddons undo                                put back what it replaced

Restores the whole WTF/ (keybindings, macros, chat and every addon's settings) as the
backup holds them; use --addon for one addon: only the SavedVariables of the folders it
had when the backup was taken, under every account and character. It refuses while the
game runs (or may be running), and where files cannot be replaced in one atomic step; it
checks the copy against the backup's hashes when it has them. Before a whole restore,
where the filesystem clones files, it keeps the current WTF/ as a backup (before
restore), and undo puts back what a restore replaced either way.
--if-match <token> restores exactly what that --dry-run showed.

See also: backup list, undo

Global options:
      --json              One JSON envelope on stdout
      --format <FORMAT>   Output format [possible values: json, human]
  -t, --target <TARGET>   The client to act on: id, game mode, family, path, or all [alias:
                          --flavor]
      --dry-run           Show the plan without changing anything
      --actor <ACTOR>     Who is acting: human, agent or widget [env: OMADDONS_ACTOR]
      --reason <TEXT>     Why, recorded verbatim in history
      --offline           Fail any network access [env: OMADDONS_OFFLINE=1]
      --while-running     Allow folder changes while the client runs (never SavedVariables)
      --if-match <TOKEN>  Run only what the preview that returned this token showed
      --no-color          No ANSI color
      --no-progress       No progress output
      --progress <MODE>   Progress events on stderr [possible values: json, human, none]
      --quiet             Only errors on stderr
  -v, --verbose...        More detail (repeatable)
  -h, --help              Show help

Learn more: omaddons robot-docs guide
